Coverage map: document-viewer Mermaid subset -> flowchart/state/sequence parser positives and unsupported negatives; labels/quoted newlines -> text tests; order/gap solver -> layered PAV behavior; required 20 docs and 20 state inputs -> fixture_counts; every .bboxy Mermaid source has a fixture and every fixture has a source -> every_bboxy_mermaid_block_has_a_fixture; real geometry -> no overlap, cluster containment, border endpoints and frame bounds; distinct links/subgraph direction -> dedicated source cases; repeatability -> fresh independent layout_is_deterministic invocations. No spec acceptance or invariant check lost coverage.

The geometry cache calls the real render parser/layout once per real fixture with the same public MonoMeasure/Style inputs as before. It names parse/layout failures during initialization. The cluster test still independently parses source, then checks geometry against its memberships. This avoids repeated setup without replacing any production algorithm with expected fixture geometry.

